\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces \textcolor {tbdc}{\textbf  {[PLACEHOLDER DATA]}}\nonbreakingspace Two frontiers on two different suites, never merged. (a) The LIBERO-Spatial forced-horizon sweep is entirely measured and is the periodic arm for that suite; it is non-monotone, which is itself a result. (b) The LIBERO-Object budget sweep places five arms at eight matched target budgets. Filled markers are the frozen blind test. At every matched send fraction, the learned trigger remains inside the confidence band of rate-matched periodic sampling, and the content-blind Bernoulli arm remains inside the learned arm's. The band is the McNemar half-width at $n=160$; arms closer together than the band are not separated by this experiment, which is the case for learned versus Bernoulli at every budget and is not the case for either against LPIPS.}}{10}{figure.caption.26}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:frontier}{{10}{10}{\synthcap Two frontiers on two different suites, never merged. (a) The LIBERO-Spatial forced-horizon sweep is entirely measured and is the periodic arm for that suite; it is non-monotone, which is itself a result. (b) The LIBERO-Object budget sweep places five arms at eight matched target budgets. Filled markers are the frozen blind test. At every matched send fraction, the learned trigger remains inside the confidence band of rate-matched periodic sampling, and the content-blind Bernoulli arm remains inside the learned arm's. The band is the McNemar half-width at $n=160$; arms closer together than the band are not separated by this experiment, which is the case for learned versus Bernoulli at every budget and is not the case for either against LPIPS}{figure.caption.26}{}}
\newlabel{fig:frontier@cref}{{[figure][10][]10}{[1][9][]10}{}{}{}}
