\newlabel{fig:agetail}{{14}{12}{\synthcap At an identical mean send rate, threshold triggering concentrates transmissions and leaves a heavier observation-age tail than periodic sampling---and, from an age of one step through six, than an unbiased coin at the same rate, which is the comparison that carries the argument. The maximum-silence safeguard truncates but does not remove the excess. Periodic and Bernoulli curves are exact, not measured, and bracket the range any scheduler at this rate can occupy}{figure.caption.30}{}}
\newlabel{fig:agetail@cref}{{[figure][14][]14}{[1][11][]12}{}{}{}}
